# Rust
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED, deliberately. The default template ignores it, which is the right call for a
# library and the wrong one here: this workspace ships a binary, and REL-1's release job builds with
# `--locked` so a tagged build resolves exactly what the gates tested. Without the lockfile in the repo
# that flag fails outright, which would have broken the first release the first time it ran.

# rust-doctor local cache
.rust-doctor-cache.json
**/.rust-doctor-cache.json

# Serena (https://github.com/oraios/serena)
# `.serena/project.yml` IS versioned — it is the shared project configuration. Serena writes its own
# `.serena/.gitignore` covering the symbol cache and local overrides, so those are not repeated here.
#
# Memories are the one deliberate departure from Serena's defaults. Serena can share them across
# sessions and users, but this repo already keeps its curated knowledge in CONTEXT.md, docs/adr/ and
# TODO.md — committing an agent-written store beside those would give the same facts two sources of
# truth, which is exactly what the glossary and ADRs exist to prevent. Serena is pointed at the
# curated docs through `initial_prompt` in project.yml instead.
.serena/memories/

# Python bytecode. New as of LINT-7 (#167): nothing under scripts/ used to be IMPORTED, so no cache was
# ever written there — `.claude/hooks/pre-bash-guard.py` now does `from guard import check`, and the
# first run of it left a `scripts/__pycache__/` in `git status`.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Debug
*.log
# …EXCEPT the test fixtures, which are inputs and not output (TEST-48, #163; caught at v0.21.0).
# `*.log` above silently swallowed `scripts/tests/test-timings/*.log` when those fixtures were added, so
# `scripts/tests/run.sh` passed locally — where the files exist because whoever wrote them made them —
# and failed in CI, where a fresh checkout has neither. Four of its 23 cases were red for five commits
# while every local run said 23 passed. `git add` gives no warning when it skips an ignored path.
!scripts/tests/**/*.log

# Agent worktrees (Claude Code) — nested checkouts, never part of the repo.
.claude/worktrees/

# TEST-45 (#153). `fuzz/` is its own workspace with its own build dir, and the corpus is DERIVED from
# the cassettes — `fuzz/seed-corpus.py` rebuilds it in milliseconds. Committing it would be a second
# copy of bytes that already live in mcp-server/tests/cassettes/, free to drift the day one is
# re-recorded. `artifacts/` is where libfuzzer writes a crashing input; if one ever appears there it is
# a finding to act on, not a file to commit.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/Cargo.lock

# The prebuilt binaries staged into the npm platform packages (REL-6, #168). They are build output —
# `.github/workflows/release.yml` downloads them from the tag's own release before publishing, and
# `scripts/bootstrap-npm.sh` does the same for the one manual bootstrap. Committing one would put a
# ~5 MB binary in git history that is already an immutable release asset, and it would be stale the
# moment the next tag builds. Only the six package.json files and the wrapper's bin/ are tracked.
/npm/*/jdwp-mcp
/npm/*/jdwp-mcp.exe
